TI  - Mixed Fair Division: A Survey
AU  - Liu, Shengxin
AU  - Lu, Xinhang
AU  - Suzuki, Mashbat
AU  - Walsh, Toby
PY  - 2024
T2  - Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research
AB  - Fair division considers the allocation of scarce resources among agents in such a way that every agent gets a fair share. It is a fundamental problem in society and has received significant attention and rapid developments from the game theory and artificial intelligence communities in recent years. The majority of the fair division literature can be divided along at least two orthogonal directions: goods versus chores, and divisible versus indivisible resources. In this survey, besides describing the state of the art, we outline a number of interesting open questions and future directions in three mixed fair division settings: (i) indivisible goods and chores, (ii) divisible and indivisible goods (mixed goods), and (iii) indivisible goods with subsidy which can be viewed like a divisible good.
